Title: Aunt Hannah
Order: 21
Production Code: 1x21

EXT. WOODS NEAR LIVINGSTON HALL - DAY

AMB: wind, dry leaves

[[Dianthe Lusk]] wanders, lost, until a cabin appears in a clearing and an old woman steps out as if she'd been expected.

AUNT HANNAH
Come in, honey, and rest.

INT. AUNT HANNAH'S CABIN - CONTINUOUS

AMB: a hearth fire

Warmed by coffee, Dianthe asks the old woman's name — and gets, instead, a question back.

AUNT HANNAH
Hain't it these arms done nussed ev'ry Livingston? I knowed your mother, child. For all you're married to Marse Aubrey, you isn't a white woman.

DIANTHE LUSK
(quietly)
I don't deny it.

With a cry, [[Hannah]] pulls her close.

AUNT HANNAH
Gawd-a-mercy — my Mira's gal!

She tells it all: raised in the big house, coerced by "young marse" — the elder Dr. Livingston — into bearing his children. Mira, her only child kept back from the block. Reuel, Mira's first. Dianthe, her second.

AUNT HANNAH (CONT'D)
Den de Doctor married a white lady, an' when she found out about Mira's children, Mira had to be sold. A week before, Misses' own baby died an hour after birth — same night Mira birthed a son. I changed the babies, honey. Told Marse Livingston that Mira's boy was the one who died. Aubrey is your own blood brother.

DIANTHE LUSK
(reeling)
My brothers. Both of them.

Hannah bares her own chest — a lotus-lily mark, the same as Dianthe's own.

AUNT HANNAH
All of Mira's children bear it. All of one blood.

Dianthe faints into the old woman's arms.
